A new version of R/qtl (1.13-7) has been released at its web site
(http://www.rqtl.org).

See http://www.rqtl.org/STATUS.txt for a list of changes.  There was
just one major change (see below).  Mostly, this was to fix some
problems that will come with the next version of R.

Karl Broman
kbr...@biostat.wisc.edu

------

Version 1.13, 9/10/2009:

Major changes:

  Fixed a bug in fitqtl regarding the case of a locus on the
  chromosome...the cited LOD scores for X chromosome loci were not
  right.  Had to make slight modifications to scanqtl, addqtl,
  addpair, addint, addcovarint, refineqtl.

